# OPNsense / pfSense-style walled garden + Classroom Desk aliases
# Create host aliases first:
#   classroom_desk_allow  — admitted client IPs (Shield allow/allowlist)
#   classroom_desk_block  — kicked / deny clients
#   classroom_desk_portal — teacher host IP(s) serving /portal + API
#
# Floating / LAN rules (conceptual order — implement in OPNsense Firewall → Rules):

# 1) Always allow DNS to DeskDNS / portal host (optional if using OPNsense DNS)
# pass in quick on $lan proto { tcp udp } from any to $classroom_desk_portal port { 53 5353 8787 }

# 2) Captive / unauthenticated: only portal + DHCP + DNS
# pass in quick on $lan proto tcp from !$classroom_desk_allow to $classroom_desk_portal port { 80 443 8787 }
# pass in quick on $lan proto udp from any to any port 53
# pass in quick on $lan proto udp from any to any port 67

# 3) Explicit block list (kick / never_student_net)
# block in quick on $lan from $classroom_desk_block to any

# 4) Admitted clients full egress (or restrict as school policy)
# pass in on $lan from $classroom_desk_allow to any

# 5) Default deny remaining LAN clients until portal admit
# block in on $lan from any to !(self|$classroom_desk_portal) 

# Notes:
# - Shield adapter writes IPs into allow/block aliases via alias_util + reconfigure.
# - openNDS can sync the same allowlist via deploy/opennds/auth_allowlist.sh
# - Screenshot checklist: see docs/OPNSENSE_ACCEPTANCE.md
